        content: '<h1>📊 Chapter 9: Volume Analysis - Complete Practical Guide</h1><h2>Theory Section: Volume Rules Every Trader Must Know</h2><div class="edu-compare-table"><thead><tr><th>Price Action</th><th>Volume</th><th>Interpretation</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Uptrend continues</th><th>Increasing volume</th><th style="color:var(--up-color);">HEALTHY - Buyers committed</th><th>Stay long, add on pullbacks</th></tr><tr><td>Uptrend continues</th><th>Decreasing volume</th><th style="color:var(--warning);">WARNING - Trend losing steam</th><th>Tighten stops, reduce size</th></tr><tr><td>Breakout above resistance</th><th>High (1.5x+ average)</th><th style="color:var(--up-color);">VALID - Likely to sustain</th><th>Enter on retest</th></tr><tr><td>Breakout above resistance</th><th>Low (below average)</th><th style="color:var(--down-color);">FALSE - Likely to fail</th><th>Wait, do NOT enter</th></tr><tr><td>Price falling, Volume rising</th><th>Increasing on down moves</th><th style="color:var(--down-color);">DISTRIBUTION - Smart money selling</th><th>Avoid longs, consider shorts</th></tr><td><td style="background:var(--accent-muted);">Volume climax at top</th><th>Extreme spike (3x-5x)</th><th style="color:var(--down-color);">EXHAUSTION - Reversal likely</th><th>Take profits, consider reversal</th></tr></tbody></div><div class="edu-strategy-card"><h4>📊 OBV (On-Balance Volume) - Professional Use</h4><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">1</span> <strong>Calculation:</strong> Cumulative - adds volume on up days, subtracts on down days</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">2</span> <strong>Rising OBV:</strong> Accumulation happening - bullish for price</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">3</span> <strong>Falling OBV:</strong> Distribution happening - bearish for price</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">4</span> <strong>OBV Divergence:</strong> Price up, OBV flat/down = bearish warning (smart money selling into strength)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">5</span> <strong>In TradeVision Pro:</strong> Search "OBV" in Indicators modal, add to separate pane</div></div><div class="edu-strategy-card"><h4>💵 MFI (Money Flow Index) - Volume-Weighted RSI</h4><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">1</span> <strong>Range:</strong> 0-100 scale, combines price AND volume</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">2</span> <strong>Overbought:</strong> MFI > 80 (volume confirms overbought)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">3</span> <strong>Oversold:</strong> MFI < 20 (volume confirms oversold)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">4</span> <strong>MFI Divergence:</strong> More powerful than RSI divergence because volume confirms</div></div><div class="edu-example-box"><div class="edu-example-label">📊 Real Volume Analysis Trade Example</div><p>BTC rallies from $50,000 to $60,000 on increasing volume (healthy).<br>At $60,000, volume spikes 3x average (volume climax).<br>OBV starts to flatten while price continues up (divergence).<br>Next red candle with high volume appears.<br><br><strong>Trade Setup (Short):</strong><br>Entry: $59,500 (on red candle close)<br>Stop: $61,000 (above climax high)<br>Target: $55,000 (previous support)<br>Reason: Smart money distributed at top, confirmed by volume climax and OBV divergence</p></div><div class="edu-strategy-card"><h4>📋 Step-by-Step: Implement Volume Analysis in Trades</h4><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">1</span> Open BTC/USDT on Daily chart</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">2</span> Add <strong>Volume</strong> indicator (bottom pane)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">3</span> Add <strong>OBV</strong> indicator (search in Indicators modal)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">4</span> Add <strong>MFI</strong> indicator (Volume category)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">5</span> Calculate 20-period average volume (visual approximation)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">6</span> Identify recent breakout - check volume relative to average</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">7</span> Check for OBV divergence (price higher but OBV lower)</div><div class="edu-step"><span class="edu-step-num">8</span> Check MFI for overbought/oversold extremes</div></div><div class="edu-practice-box" style="background:rgba(124,58,237,0.08); border:2px solid #7c3aed; border-radius:12px; padding:20px; margin:20px 0;"><strong>📝 PRACTICE EXERCISE #9:</strong><br><br>1. Open any cryptocurrency chart with Volume, OBV, MFI indicators<br>2. Find a breakout and confirm with volume (1.5x+ average)<br>3. Find a false breakout (price broke but volume below average)<br>4. Look for volume climax (3x+ average in last 20 candles)<br>5. Find OBV divergence (price higher, OBV lower OR price lower, OBV higher)<br>6. Place a PAPER trade where:<br>   - Volume confirms breakout<br>   - OBV confirms direction<br>   - MFI is not at extreme<br>   - Calculate R:R before entering<br><br><strong>✅ Success Criteria:</strong> You can read volume to confirm/reject breakouts, spot distribution/accumulation, and identify volume climaxes that signal reversals</div>'
